※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=21 diag=none

※ A variable of an array type at the top level holds the elements themselves,
※ which are bytes in the image like any other variable's value.  Every element
※ has to be one the compiler knows, for the same reason.

let table: u8⟦5⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 4u8, 8u8, 16u8⟧

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    table⟦0⟧ + table⟦2⟧ + table⟦4⟧
